course: dictionary
lesson: 8846
title: Shivering: cold, fear or fever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shivering means shaking a little, quickly and without meaning to. Most often it happens because you are cold. «The shivering, sunless days!» tells you the days are cold and grey, so people shake to keep warm.
explain: Shivering can also show fear or excitement. «She stood shivering at the top of the high diving board.» She is not cold here. She shakes because she is scared. Read the words around the word, because they tell you which kind of shivering it is.
explain: Shivering can also happen when you are ill with a fever. But strong shivering in cold weather can be a warning. «Strong shivering, slurred words and clumsiness are warning signs that the body is getting dangerously cold» so tell a grown-up straight away.
fact: Shivering means shaking a little, often because you are cold.
fact: Shivering is your body's way of making heat: your muscles shake quickly to warm you up.
fact: You can also shiver with fear, with excitement, or when you have a fever.
fact: «Shivering with cold» and «shivering with fear» show the reason for the shaking.
fact: A shivering person who is cold needs warm dry clothes, a blanket and shelter.
exercise: «The shivering, sunless days!» What does shivering tell you about the days? | They are full of loud music | They are very short | They are hot and sunny | *They are cold
exercise: «She stood shivering at the top of the high diving board.» Why is she shivering? | Because she is too hot in the sun | *Because she is scared | Because she has won a prize | Because she is asleep
exercise: A friend is shivering hard after falling into cold water. What should you do first? | Tell them to stop shivering | *Get them into warm dry clothes and wrap them in a blanket | Tell them to swim again to warm up | Leave them to rest in wet clothes
test: When your body shivers, what is it doing to keep you warm? | Your skin turns green | Your bones grow longer | Your blood stops moving so you cool down | *Your muscles shake quickly to make heat
test: Which phrase shows shaking because of fear? | «warm and dry» | «sunless days» | *«shivering with fear» | «a warm blanket»
exam: Which of these is a warning sign that the body is getting dangerously cold? | *Strong shivering, slurred words and clumsiness | Feeling warm and sleepy in a sunny garden | A short, gentle breeze on your face | Smiling and singing a happy song
